WEBVTT

00:04.420 --> 00:08.230
Now then, what should I make tonight?

00:08.570 --> 00:11.860
I know Mana said she wanted to eat curry.

00:45.700 --> 00:48.340
What on Earth?

00:49.440 --> 00:50.740
What happened?

01:02.380 --> 01:06.020
Was that actually a spatial quake?

02:48.750 --> 02:53.490
<i>All citizens, please remain indoors 
until instructed otherwise!</i>

02:53.490 --> 02:56.370
<i>Also, airwaves are being overloaded,</i>

02:56.370 --> 02:59.570
<i>so please do your part 
by refraining from using phones</i>

02:57.220 --> 03:02.160
Big Brother! I'm so glad to see you... safe?

02:59.570 --> 03:01.080
<i>and other communication devices</i>

03:01.080 --> 03:02.160
<i>as much as possible!</i>

03:02.160 --> 03:04.210
<i>We ask that you please remain calm!</i>

03:06.940 --> 03:08.160
Big Brother?

03:08.160 --> 03:10.440
Mana?! Well, you see, this is—

03:10.440 --> 03:13.280
Don't worry! I'm on your side, Big Brother!

03:13.280 --> 03:16.060
Let's take our time to repent 
for the sins you've committed!

03:16.060 --> 03:18.140
Nothing you're assuming is okay!

03:19.500 --> 03:21.260
I understand the situation.

03:21.600 --> 03:22.620
But still!

03:22.620 --> 03:25.260
That didn't mean you had to 
bring her to our place!

03:25.680 --> 03:27.800
What else could I do?

03:27.800 --> 03:31.130
The city's in a panic, 
and she won't say anything to me,

03:31.130 --> 03:33.270
so I had no idea what I should do.

03:33.270 --> 03:34.150
Achoo!

03:35.510 --> 03:38.230
For starters, let's have her wear my clothes!

03:38.650 --> 03:40.670
I'll go get some right now, so—

03:51.250 --> 03:52.240
Huh?

03:53.620 --> 03:55.630
Danger Do Not Cross

04:00.130 --> 04:03.010
<b>Fafner
in the Azure</b>

04:00.130 --> 04:03.010
History and Economics

04:03.010 --> 04:04.250
I see.

04:04.800 --> 04:07.510
I mostly have the language system down now.

04:08.970 --> 04:10.020
What's the matter?

04:10.320 --> 04:12.880
What do you mean? You just—

04:12.880 --> 04:17.760
"Ah" and "Unh" were all 
you could say yesterday,

04:17.760 --> 04:20.030
and now you're suddenly speaking fluently,

04:20.030 --> 04:22.100
so of course we'd be surprised.

04:22.100 --> 04:24.960
You're using more proper Japanese than Mana.

04:24.960 --> 04:25.530
Hmm?!

04:26.840 --> 04:32.330
Big Brother, I think you might be saying 
only "ah" and "unh" for a while.

04:32.330 --> 04:33.960
Wait! Calm down!

04:33.960 --> 04:36.350
I love how unique you are!

04:36.350 --> 04:38.000
So long as you understand.

04:38.820 --> 04:44.010
By the way, I'd like to ask, 
but who exactly are you?

04:44.360 --> 04:47.140
You're clearly not a normal person.

04:47.140 --> 04:51.220
Does yesterday's spatial quake 
have any connection to you?

04:52.100 --> 04:54.390
I'm sorry, I don't know.

04:56.750 --> 04:59.370
It doesn't seem like she's lying.

04:59.370 --> 05:02.510
Then could you tell us 
what you do know at least?

05:03.010 --> 05:05.530
Um, I'd like to know more about you.

05:06.330 --> 05:08.150
What I remember...

05:08.150 --> 05:13.110
is a vast horizon following some kind of 
explosion like the one from yesterday.

05:13.540 --> 05:16.040
There were three people there.

05:16.480 --> 05:19.980
Two young men and one little girl.

05:19.980 --> 05:21.850
Three people?

05:21.850 --> 05:24.360
Following an explosion like yesterday's?

05:24.360 --> 05:27.180
You were there at 
the Great Eurasian Spatial Quake?

05:30.210 --> 05:32.380
A-Are you okay?

05:32.380 --> 05:36.330
I'm fine. I just felt a little pain.

05:36.330 --> 05:39.190
I see. Please don't push yourself.

05:41.380 --> 05:42.690
Thank you.

05:44.090 --> 05:44.820
Ah!

05:45.280 --> 05:49.780
So, Big Brother, what are you 
planning to do with this woman?

05:50.650 --> 05:52.370
What will I do?

05:52.370 --> 05:53.260
The police should—

05:53.260 --> 05:54.440
N-No, wait!

05:54.440 --> 05:57.640
Both hospitals and the police 
are busy after yesterday.

05:57.640 --> 06:00.460
If we just tossed her into their care 
without warning, then...

06:01.540 --> 06:03.060
I know.

06:03.060 --> 06:06.610
I guess we'll just wait and see 
for now while she stays with us?

06:06.610 --> 06:09.090
It doesn't seem like she's a bad person.

06:11.150 --> 06:13.600
You're going to let me stay here?

06:13.600 --> 06:14.680
Yes.

06:14.680 --> 06:17.740
Since our father and mother 
aren't here right now.

06:18.290 --> 06:19.640
Uh...

06:19.640 --> 06:22.740
That reminds me, we haven't 
introduced ourselves, have we?

06:22.740 --> 06:25.110
Neither of us have shared our names.

06:25.460 --> 06:26.720
Names?

06:26.720 --> 06:29.410
That's right. I'm Shinji Takamiya,

06:29.410 --> 06:30.760
and this is my little sister,

06:30.760 --> 06:32.570
Mana Takamiya.

06:32.570 --> 06:35.330
Shinji and Mana Takamiya...

06:35.330 --> 06:37.380
So, what's your name?

06:37.380 --> 06:39.750
You do have a name, right?

06:41.510 --> 06:44.470
My name?

06:45.750 --> 06:49.480
Uh, you don't need to force 
yourself to remember.

06:49.480 --> 06:52.690
Your memories might naturally 
come back on their own in time.

06:53.150 --> 06:55.810
But it's inconvenient 
if she doesn't have a name.

06:55.810 --> 06:58.020
We need something to call her.

06:58.500 --> 07:01.300
In that case, well...

07:01.900 --> 07:03.400
<b>May</b>

07:03.880 --> 07:05.770
I know, Mio!

07:06.090 --> 07:07.090
Mio?

07:07.090 --> 07:10.280
Mio, written with zero and 
the water radical to make waterway.

07:10.280 --> 07:13.000
Oh, that's not bad.

07:13.000 --> 07:14.280
By the way, how did you come up with that?

07:14.280 --> 07:18.480
Well, yesterday was May 30th, right?

07:18.480 --> 07:21.140
So 3-0 can be read as Mio.

07:24.540 --> 07:25.430
Mio.

07:25.790 --> 07:28.410
Still, we have public 
appearances to worry about,

07:28.410 --> 07:31.460
so for a while we'll say 
you're a family member.

07:31.940 --> 07:35.550
Meaning your full name will be Mio Takamiya!

07:36.990 --> 07:38.710
Mio Takamiya?

07:44.560 --> 07:45.620
Huh?

07:45.950 --> 07:47.650
That's strange.

07:47.650 --> 07:50.460
I'm happy, so why am I...?

07:51.410 --> 07:52.570
This is...

08:02.070 --> 08:03.330
Hey, Ike.

08:03.700 --> 08:06.300
Do you really think she's in this town?

08:06.910 --> 08:09.590
She might have run away 
somewhere else already.

08:10.020 --> 08:13.370
I just hope she's safe at least.

08:34.820 --> 08:36.570
All right!

08:38.580 --> 08:40.370
I finally nabbed it.

08:41.290 --> 08:42.580
Here you go, Mio.

08:42.900 --> 08:43.690
Huh?

08:45.020 --> 08:46.580
You're giving it to me?

08:46.580 --> 08:48.920
That's why I nabbed it.

08:48.920 --> 08:51.170
Or did you not want it?

08:51.170 --> 08:55.090
You kept looking at it during our walk, 
so I assumed you love stuff like this.

08:56.100 --> 08:57.070
Love...

08:58.110 --> 08:59.200
Love...

08:59.200 --> 09:01.270
To view something favorably...

09:01.790 --> 09:04.730
To be drawn to something 
with strong interest...

09:05.350 --> 09:06.840
That's it!

09:06.840 --> 09:09.250
Yeah, I'm sure this is love!

09:10.300 --> 09:13.110
I love you!

09:18.070 --> 09:19.620
Uh, Mio.

09:19.620 --> 09:21.790
If you'd like, would you go on a

09:22.420 --> 09:24.700
d-date with me?!

09:27.020 --> 09:29.220
I should practice a bit more.

09:30.000 --> 09:31.730
G-Good morning, Mio.

09:31.730 --> 09:32.970
Nice weather we're having, huh?

09:32.970 --> 09:34.630
Want to go out for a bit?

09:35.000 --> 09:36.350
No, that's not right.

09:36.350 --> 09:39.690
We go shopping together all the time anyway.

09:40.100 --> 09:41.640
I want it to be more.

09:41.640 --> 09:43.140
A real date.

09:43.140 --> 09:46.270
I want Mio to think of it as a date, too.

09:46.690 --> 09:48.410
Uh, ahem, ahem.

09:48.930 --> 09:51.690
Mio, let's go on a date.

09:51.690 --> 09:52.390
Sure!

09:52.770 --> 09:54.360
M-Mio?!

09:54.360 --> 09:56.430
Yeah? What's the matter, Shin?

09:56.430 --> 09:58.660
H-How long have you been there?

09:58.660 --> 10:02.070
Since you said, "No, that's not right."

10:02.530 --> 10:05.580
So, Shin, when are we going?

10:05.580 --> 10:07.790
Huh? G-Going on what?

10:08.150 --> 10:10.290
On our date.

10:11.490 --> 10:12.540
A date?!

10:12.540 --> 10:13.370
Yeah.

10:13.910 --> 10:16.170
Y-You're going on a date?!

10:16.170 --> 10:20.460
My shy, unsociable big brother 
asked you out on a date?!

10:23.560 --> 10:24.830
Yeah.

10:24.830 --> 10:27.170
Though thinking about it,

10:27.170 --> 10:31.020
a date is just a man and woman 
meeting up together, right?

10:32.070 --> 10:34.790
I'm with Shin every day,

10:34.790 --> 10:40.570
so I'm not really sure what it means to 
go out together in a more formal sense.

10:40.570 --> 10:43.050
Well, in short it means big brother

10:43.050 --> 10:46.200
wants to grow even closer to you, Mio!

10:46.690 --> 10:49.940
You could say he's trying to 
show you his affection.

10:51.980 --> 10:52.960
Mio?

10:53.540 --> 10:55.060
I see!

10:55.060 --> 10:58.290
Shin feels affection toward me...

10:58.290 --> 10:59.970
That makes me happy.

11:04.540 --> 11:05.470
Jeez!

11:06.720 --> 11:07.610
All right!

11:07.610 --> 11:10.350
In that case, let's get you prepared!

11:11.060 --> 11:13.200
I heard what's going on!

11:13.200 --> 11:16.110
I'm Haruko Homura, Mana's BFF!

11:16.110 --> 11:18.680
Leave this to me!

11:18.680 --> 11:20.140
BFF?

11:20.140 --> 11:24.370
Yeah, it's not in the dictionary, 
so don't worry about the word.

11:24.370 --> 11:28.420
Haruko knows a lot about fashion, 
so I called her in to help.

11:29.250 --> 11:32.370
I know you told me before, 
but she really is a pretty woman.

11:32.820 --> 11:37.200
Who's the lucky boy who's 
getting to date such a beauty?

11:37.200 --> 11:39.380
Well, my big brother.

11:39.380 --> 11:39.920
Huh?!

11:39.920 --> 11:42.260
For real?! Way to go!

11:42.940 --> 11:44.900
All right, I've got it!

11:44.900 --> 11:48.010
This is going to be well worth it 
in all kinds of ways!

11:48.450 --> 11:51.640
First, I need to equip my focus enhancing item!

11:54.780 --> 11:56.900
Now which should we go with?

11:57.650 --> 12:01.530
U-Um, I'm counting on you.

12:07.250 --> 12:08.370
Shin...

12:20.100 --> 12:22.780
What's the matter? You had a scary look...

12:23.420 --> 12:24.880
S-Sorry.

12:24.880 --> 12:26.900
Did I look that scary?

12:26.900 --> 12:28.290
You did.

12:28.290 --> 12:30.590
You looked like you were 
going off to war or something.

12:31.110 --> 12:33.010
War, huh?

12:34.150 --> 12:37.050
Sorry, I was spacing out.

12:37.050 --> 12:40.940
It's just... y-you're way too cute!

12:47.730 --> 12:49.690
W-Well, then...

12:51.220 --> 12:52.270
Shall we go?

12:54.690 --> 12:55.460
Yeah!

12:55.930 --> 12:59.150
Shall we start our date?

13:08.520 --> 13:09.940
The ocean...

13:09.940 --> 13:12.740
You said you wanted to see it 
someday, right?

13:12.740 --> 13:14.140
I'm so happy!

13:14.140 --> 13:15.810
Thank you, Shin!

13:15.810 --> 13:19.110
Yeah, I'm glad that you're enjoying it.

13:23.700 --> 13:24.610
Mio!

13:25.420 --> 13:26.560
Wow!

13:27.610 --> 13:28.560
Mio!

13:28.560 --> 13:29.870
The hem of your skirt is—

13:30.830 --> 13:31.620
Shin!

13:37.120 --> 13:38.000
Mio!

13:39.850 --> 13:42.130
H-Hey, Mio!

13:56.260 --> 13:57.560
M-Mio?!

14:14.550 --> 14:15.580
Achoo!

14:31.210 --> 14:33.530
What are we doing for dinner tonight?

14:33.530 --> 14:35.210
I haven't decided yet.

14:35.210 --> 14:37.480
Is there anything you'd like to eat, Mio?

14:37.930 --> 14:40.850
I'm happy with any food you make, Shin.

14:44.350 --> 14:45.230
Mio?

14:53.240 --> 14:54.620
This way!

14:54.620 --> 14:57.620
Mio! What's gotten into you?!

14:57.620 --> 14:59.250
I'll explain later!

14:59.250 --> 15:00.530
Hurry!

15:13.070 --> 15:14.890
Who are you people?!

15:15.830 --> 15:18.270
Shin, grab on to me!

15:18.270 --> 15:19.170
Huh?!

15:28.180 --> 15:28.860
Shin!

15:29.230 --> 15:31.610
I'm all right. We need to hurry!

15:40.610 --> 15:41.820
Show me your hand.

15:56.010 --> 15:56.850
Huh?

15:56.850 --> 15:58.150
Hey!

15:58.830 --> 15:59.550
Shh!

16:07.300 --> 16:09.850
Who on earth were those guys?

16:09.850 --> 16:12.680
They're probably after me.

16:12.680 --> 16:13.580
Huh?!

16:13.580 --> 16:15.340
I've started to remember.

16:15.910 --> 16:19.530
When I first woke up that man 
from before was in front of me.

16:20.140 --> 16:22.740
Then he tried to capture me.

16:24.490 --> 16:25.530
I'm sorry.

16:25.940 --> 16:28.610
It's my fault you've gotten wrapped up in this.

16:29.260 --> 16:30.260
Run.

16:30.260 --> 16:31.250
I'll handle the rest.

16:31.250 --> 16:32.350
No way!

16:34.970 --> 16:38.010
I was ready to face some trouble

16:38.260 --> 16:40.770
from the moment I took in a girl 
with mysterious powers.

16:43.390 --> 16:46.420
We're family now.

16:51.530 --> 16:54.390
Anyway, let's slip out to where 
there are lots of people.

16:54.390 --> 16:55.910
Then we'll go to the police.

16:56.530 --> 16:58.530
Don't underestimate the rule of law!

17:03.220 --> 17:04.410
Get back!

17:04.740 --> 17:05.700
Mio!

17:05.700 --> 17:07.670
Don't worry, I won't kill him!

17:08.130 --> 17:10.830
Hey now, are you serious?

17:10.830 --> 17:14.420
Why would you to come to me of all places?

17:14.420 --> 17:15.610
Huh?!

17:16.790 --> 17:19.100
Hmm, so is Mio that woman's name?

17:19.100 --> 17:21.060
Yeah, I gave it to her.

17:21.340 --> 17:24.230
I see. It's a good name.

17:24.790 --> 17:27.060
Hey, are you happy right now?

17:27.420 --> 17:32.940
At the very least, I don't enjoy being 
chased around by people hostile to me!

17:33.330 --> 17:36.340
No, I'm not referring to that.

17:36.340 --> 17:38.700
I was talking about being 
with that guy beside you.

17:42.670 --> 17:43.650
I see.

17:47.450 --> 17:48.330
Then scram.

17:49.590 --> 17:50.840
What's the meaning of this?

17:51.740 --> 17:53.680
There's nothing else to it.

17:53.680 --> 17:55.260
Hurry up and go already.

17:58.750 --> 18:03.150
Boy... Take care of that girl, Mio.

18:13.300 --> 18:15.810
It's been a long time, Spirit.

18:16.270 --> 18:17.700
I've missed you.

18:19.890 --> 18:22.750
It's my first time meeting that boy there.

18:23.390 --> 18:27.300
Thank you for taking care of our Spirit.

18:27.300 --> 18:29.210
I truly am grateful.

18:29.210 --> 18:30.320
Don't give me that!

18:30.320 --> 18:32.630
We have your little sister in custody.

18:34.180 --> 18:37.260
Now, why don't we return 
both women to where they belong?

18:37.260 --> 18:38.370
Why you!

18:38.370 --> 18:39.850
Just try doing anything to Mana!

18:39.850 --> 18:41.140
I'll never forgive you if you do!

18:41.140 --> 18:45.100
Oh? Her name is Mana, then?

18:45.100 --> 18:47.180
That's quite the joke.

18:47.710 --> 18:51.620
I can understand why our Spirit 
would wind up there.

18:55.290 --> 18:56.470
Promise me.

18:56.970 --> 18:59.700
If I go with you, then you'll return Mana.

19:01.580 --> 19:03.950
Yes, of course we will.

19:04.650 --> 19:05.580
Mio?!

19:05.580 --> 19:06.720
It's okay.

19:06.720 --> 19:09.960
I was never supposed to exist here anyway.

19:11.030 --> 19:14.710
Even spending a short time 
with you made me happy.

19:26.780 --> 19:27.720
Screw that!

19:28.350 --> 19:30.250
Screw that!

19:31.150 --> 19:32.850
Shin! What are you—?!

19:32.850 --> 19:33.940
Idiot!

19:33.940 --> 19:36.130
Do you really think he'll keep his promise?!

19:36.130 --> 19:40.780
What guarantee do we have that he won't 
just kill me and Mana once we has you, Mio?!

19:41.530 --> 19:45.370
So as long as you're with us, 
they can't lay a hand on Mana!

19:45.370 --> 19:48.690
So it would be way better to stay 
with me and shore up our position!

20:01.890 --> 20:02.950
Shin?

20:03.430 --> 20:04.430
Good grief.

20:05.390 --> 20:08.680
I wasn't actually lying, you know.

20:08.680 --> 20:09.690
Shin!

20:13.530 --> 20:14.310
Mi...

20:20.370 --> 20:21.150
o...

21:16.070 --> 21:17.670
Right.

21:18.090 --> 21:20.170
I can just recreate him.

21:39.330 --> 21:42.150
I'll never let go of you again.

21:42.830 --> 21:45.450
I won't make any more mistakes.

21:46.750 --> 21:47.700
So...

21:51.130 --> 21:52.700
wait for me,

21:52.700 --> 21:53.930
Shin.

21:52.700 --> 21:54.960
<b>Episode 4</b>

21:52.700 --> 21:54.960
<b>The Spirit's Resurrection</b>

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
Episode 5 "Mother Mio"

23:25.960 --> 23:28.860
Mio Takamiya, 
the mother of all Spirits.

23:28.860 --> 23:30.090
As the battle rages on,

23:30.090 --> 23:31.660
some confront their most beloved

23:31.660 --> 23:33.970
and others confront their hated enemies.

23:33.970 --> 23:36.810
Next episode is Episode 5: "Mother Mio."

23:36.810 --> 23:39.690
The blossoms of death bloom in the sky.
